                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Not recommended at the insane price of $34.99 with greedy microtransactions. In my opinion, MSRP should have been set around $9.99-$14.99, and even then, I would wait for a sale.\n\nThis is an RPG Maker game: the usual low resolution, funky keybindings, etc. A diablo-like action RPG, and it does that okayish (being generous here.) Not good, not bad. I played it for almost 2 hours and did not have much fun. It's not very challenging (you can AFK button mash,) and the story is slow and not good enough for me to care. \n\nThe problem is that there are so many much better action RPGs in terms of gameplay and story for a much better price. Examples would be The Diablo Eternal Collection at $39.99 MSRP, Path of Exiles - free, Grim Dawn at $24.99 MSRP, Book of Demons at $24.99 MSRP, and the list goes on. \n\nOn top of the crazy high MSRP, there are DLC Microtransactions for in-game consumables. This is a single-player RPG, not an online game you can play with friends. Why are devs charging $1-4 for in-game materials and consumables? Is the game not balanced? Did the devs make the game more grindy so you'd pay to skip? It's hilarious that this game has $73.70 worth of consumable DLC. As it's a single-player game, just download CheatEngine and add the stuff to the game yourself for free. \n\nI looked into the game and see that this was a Kickstarter project from years ago. So kudos to the devs for going through with the project and delivering, But it's going to need a lot of work, content, and repricing to make this a worthwhile purchase. The original Kickstarter price of 1500 JPY would have been a reasonable ask, so I'm confused why the devs jacked up the game to cost over $100 for the complete edition. With all the DLC, this game is more expensive than all the current triple-A titles, including deluxe editions.",
